        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Tjy3gFDsrtvGEef3QPxYsR",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/circuit-breaker.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Circuit Breaker\\ndescription: A state machine pattern that prevents cascading failure by wrapping calls to unreliable dependencies with fault tolerance logic.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Circuit-Breaker\\n  - concept/Fault-Tolerance\\n  - concept/Resilience\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source; describes the core pattern and state transitions.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nThe **circuit breaker** pattern wraps calls to an unreliable or struggling dependency with a state machine that manages whether requests are attempted at all. It prevents cascading failure by stopping unnecessary calls while the downstream service recovers.\\n\\n## State Machine\\n\\nThe circuit breaker operates in three states:\\n\\n1. **Closed** \\u2014 Normal operation. Calls pass through to the dependency. Failures are tracked; if a failure threshold is crossed, the breaker transitions to open.\\n\\n2. **Open** \\u2014 Failure threshold exceeded. Calls fail immediately without reaching the dependency (fail-fast), allowing the struggling service room to recover without additional load.\\n\\n3. **Half-Open** \\u2014 Recovery probe. After a timeout in the open state, the breaker enters half-open and allows a trial call to the dependency. The result of that trial call decides whether to:\\n   - **Close** again if the trial succeeds, resuming normal operation.\\n   - **Return to open** if the trial fails, continuing to protect the downstream service.\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\nThe circuit breaker prevents cascading failure \\u2014 where one failing service pulls down others that depend on it \\u2014 by decoupling the caller from a struggling dependency. It gives the downstream service an opportunity to recover without being hammered by repeated request attempts.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Circuit breaker pattern description from eval://steering-adoption/sample-06\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
